{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/56156-comparison-to-blood-smoke","id":56156,"title":"Comparison to Blood & Smoke","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-23T08:33:37-08:00","id":56156,"title":"Comparison to Blood & Smoke","content":"Having read <b>Blood &amp; Smoke</b> and <b>Demon</b> back-to-back, I was struck by how much better written the former is. The writing is tighter, the rules are clearer, and there seems to be more to it. Demon is more like I expect White Wolf books to be: there is a lot of repetition, the rules are unclear and often seem untested, and there seems to be a lot of padding to make up length. Since I know a lot of the same people worked on both books, I'm curious as to the difference. I know that B&amp;S went through a period of public development which (unless I missed it) Demon didn't, and I wonder if that made the difference? Not trying to make anyone feel bad, mind you. Demon is an immensely creative work with a lot of really cool, novel ideas. I love the concepts. I just sort of wish it was as slick as B&amp;S. Am I alone in this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T09:23:22-08:00","id":56181,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest thing to keep in mind is that B&amp;S is a refinement of a game that's been around for almost ten years, while Demon is a brand new thing.<br /> <br /> This is especially important on the very subjective issues of things like repetition and &quot;padding.&quot; B&amp;S isn't trying to sell people on a new concept. It isn't trying to explain something that the other nWOD books have never really done before. It isn't trying to find a &quot;voice&quot; for the game-line. Demon, on the other hand, is trying to sell people on a new concept, explaining things that haven't been done before in the nWOD, and finding its unique voice. Repetition makes it easier for the authors to feel that they're being clear to the readers. If one section is a bit unclear on something, you have a repetition that can present it slightly differently that might click.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T09:25:44-08:00","id":56184,"title":"","content":"I think a big difference between the two is the age of the lines. Blood and Smoke is the ultimate evolution of the White Wolf Vampire game, and its rules are polished by the experience of writers and players going all the way back to the founding of the company. <br /> <br /> Demon's new. We've never had a techgnostic spy game in either WoD, and so that game is full of ambition and experimentation. Some of those ideas have iffy (I say this because I haven't tried them), implementation, such as storyteller generated player powers (interlocks), over the top powers, and a devil may care attitude toward balance. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I can't wait to play/run both games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}